    S(1, 1, "Profit and loss", "Rakesh buys a bicycle for ₹3,200 and sells it for ₹3,680. What is his profit percentage?",
      ["15%", "12%", "13%", "14%"],
      "Profit = 3,680 - 3,200 = ₹480. Profit % is worked out on the cost: 480 / 3,200 x 100 = 15%. Dividing by the selling price instead gives about 13%, a common slip."),
    S(1, 3, "Profit and loss", "By selling 12 pens for ₹90, a shopkeeper loses 10%. At what price should he sell 12 pens to gain 20%?",
      ["₹120", "₹108", "₹110", "₹115"],
      "At a 10% loss, ₹90 is 90% of the cost, so 12 pens cost ₹100. For a 20% gain he must sell them for 100 x 1.2 = ₹120."),
